meta {
  name: Submit App
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apps/{{appSlug}}/submit
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
}

docs {
  Transitions the latest draft (or needs_changes) AppVersion to
  `submitted`, making it eligible for auditor review. Also transitions
  the App itself if it was still in draft / needs_changes.

  Auditors from a DIFFERENT org than the developer can then claim the
  submission from the audit queue. Same-org auditors are blocked
  server-side (enforced on the decision endpoint).

  Validation:
    - Developer role + owning-org check.
    - App must exist and be owned by the caller's org.

  Responses:
    200 OK   — { state: "submitted", app_version_id: "<uuid>" }
    401      — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden — caller does not own this app
    404 not_found — app slug not found
    409 already_submitted    — app is already awaiting audit review
    409 no_submittable_version — no draft or needs_changes version exists;
                                 create a new version first
}
